# Compiler output. Every file here is produced from a `.rgr` in gallery/evg by
# an npm script that compiles before it runs — `evg:test`, `evg:trace:test`,
# `evg:compile` and the rest — so a fresh clone builds them and never needs
# them committed.
#
# This used to say `bin/`, which ignores a nested `bin/` directory that does
# not exist, so seventeen build artifacts were tracked. They were not harmless:
# every branch that touched EVG recompiled them, and two branches that touched
# EVG conflicted in a generated file neither of them had edited. The
# `evg_trace_cli` outputs for Python, C++ and Rust were already ignored a few
# lines apart in the root .gitignore — only the JavaScript one was kept, and
# for no reason anybody wrote down.
#
# This is the same rule gallery/ui/bin, gallery/vela/bin, gallery/book/bin and
# gallery/css/bin already use.
*
!.gitignore
